.Dd October 25, 2026
.Dt BCM2711_I2C 4D
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm bcm2711_i2c
.Nd Broadcom BCM2711 I2C controller driver
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
driver supports the Broadcom Serial Controller
.Pq BSC
I2C controllers found in the BCM2711 SoC used by the Raspberry Pi 4.
.Pp
The
.Nm
driver is part of the system's I2C framework and is accessible
through common tools such as
.Xr i2cadm 8 .
The controller supports I2C transfers to devices with 7-bit addresses,
including a write followed by a read with a repeated start condition.
SMBus operations are translated into I2C transfers by the framework.
Transfers of up to 256 bytes in each direction are supported.
.Pp
The controller operates at either 100 kHz or 400 kHz.
The initial speed is taken from the
.Sy clock-frequency
property of the controller's device tree node, defaulting to 100 kHz,
and can be changed with the
.Cm speed
controller property.
The bus clock is derived from the SoC's core clock and so scales with it
if the firmware changes the core clock.
.Pp
When the controller attaches, the driver applies the default pin
configuration from its device tree node, which switches the pins used for
the bus to their I2C function.
.Pp
On the Raspberry Pi 4, the I2C bus on the GPIO header is disabled unless
it is enabled in the firmware configuration, for example by adding
.Ql dtparam=i2c_arm=on
to
.Pa config.txt .
.Sh ARCHITECTURE
.Sy aarch64
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Pa
.It Pa /platform/RaspberryPi,4/kernel/drv/aarch64/bcm2711_i2c
Device driver (aarch64)
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr i2cadm 8
